// Seq
// The part of Seq that every other module needs: enough to build a sequence and to see its
// element type. Seq's own file (67_seq_mod.types) has the rest. Split out because `Seq.t` appears
// in Option, List, String, Hashtbl and a dozen more modules, while Seq's own examples need lists,
// arrays and options, so `seq_mod` can only come last; without this group every earlier module
// commits `Seq` with no parameter. See DEVIATIONS.md.
// type 'a t = unit -> 'a node
val empty : 'a t
val return : 'a -> 'a t
val cons : 'a -> 'a t -> 'a t
val is_empty : 'a t -> bool
val length : 'a t -> int
val for_all : ('a -> bool) -> 'a t -> bool
